WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.540
- Tell me the funniest thing you've done

00:00:01.540 --> 00:00:03.360
to get into character.

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:04.440
And I know the answer already,

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:05.660
but I just want you to tell everyone.

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:06.790
- Which one, the farting?

00:00:06.790 --> 00:00:07.799
Or was, erm--

00:00:07.799 --> 00:00:08.632
(laughs)

00:00:08.632 --> 00:00:09.840
'Cause that's not intentional.

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:12.583
What, for Margaret?

00:00:12.583 --> 00:00:13.416
- Yes.

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:15.790
- Which one, head back?

00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:17.300
I do a bit of head back.

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:19.930
- No, who did you
approach to help you get--

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:20.763
- Oh, the medium.

00:00:20.763 --> 00:00:21.970
- Yeah.

00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:23.780
- I still think that's really funny.

00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:24.613
- It's a bit.

00:00:24.613 --> 00:00:25.522
- I love you very much.

00:00:25.522 --> 00:00:26.691
(laughs)

00:00:26.691 --> 00:00:27.524
- Why not?

00:00:27.524 --> 00:00:28.720
- Did you hear, someone in
the last press junket said,

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:29.777
so they spoke to, said,

00:00:29.777 --> 00:00:32.747
"So we heard Helena approached a medium,

00:00:32.747 --> 00:00:33.770
"did you approach a medium?"

00:00:33.770 --> 00:00:34.800
No, 'cause

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:36.070
- She's alive!
- the Queen's still alive!

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:38.532
- Somebody yesterday did
say, really, really clever,

00:00:38.532 --> 00:00:41.207
lovely man, photographer, said like

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:42.987
"So, did you get to meet her?

00:00:42.987 --> 00:00:44.221
"Did you have to meet--"

00:00:44.221 --> 00:00:45.452
(laughs)

00:00:45.452 --> 00:00:48.111
- Kind of, he did, but--

00:00:48.111 --> 00:00:49.902
- Kind of.

00:00:49.902 --> 00:00:54.490
- But, no, I'm very anal
so no stone unturned,

00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:55.800
so I thought, well why not?

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:56.880
Give it a whirl,
- Yeah!

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:58.530
- Meet a medium, and see
what they come up with.

00:00:58.530 --> 00:00:59.363
And actually, a note--

00:00:59.363 --> 00:01:00.770
- Was it helpful, though?

00:01:00.770 --> 00:01:02.490
- I think it was, 'cause first of all,

00:01:02.490 --> 00:01:05.390
the first thing that she said, was--

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:06.450
- The medium, or Margaret?

00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:07.410
- Well, it was via the medium,

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:09.580
obviously Margaret wasn't to spare,

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:11.460
but the medium, who is a friend of mine,

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:13.300
who's done, who's a psychic, and genuinely

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:14.843
helps people--
- And did then get paid?

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:18.970
- She did get paid, but
not an inordinate amount.

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:21.069
So don't, I know where your head's going.

00:01:21.069 --> 00:01:22.530
(laughs)

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:24.110
Take total advantage of me.

00:01:24.110 --> 00:01:27.160
So the first thing that
she said, apparently,

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:29.020
she said "Oh, Margaret's
here", and I said "Oh, really?"

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:31.150
I was actually doing it for other reasons.

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:31.983
And she said,

00:01:31.983 --> 00:01:34.230
"Oh well, we might as well
talk to her, since she's come."

00:01:34.230 --> 00:01:35.990
and said, "She's in full regalia."

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:39.270
She said she does like
the fact that I'm playing,

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:41.120
I'm a better choice to the other actor

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:42.069
they were thinking of.

00:01:42.069 --> 00:01:43.570
(scandalized gasp)

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:44.539
So, that's good.

00:01:44.539 --> 00:01:47.052
- Unless the other actor's watching this.

00:01:47.052 --> 00:01:49.266
- Well, I don't know, no, I know.

00:01:49.266 --> 00:01:52.400
But that's a very typical thing,
she gives you a compliment,

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:54.750
and then also sort of puts
you down at the same time.

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:57.750
She said it was about
time that I scrubbed up,

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:58.870
that's very Margaret, she said

00:01:58.870 --> 00:02:02.870
- Or was it your friend,
just wanting to say.

00:02:02.870 --> 00:02:03.783
- Maybe.

00:02:03.783 --> 00:02:06.300
(laughs)

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:08.790
Funnily enough, when she
contacted my great granny,

00:02:08.790 --> 00:02:10.517
my great granny had the
same thing, it's like

00:02:10.517 --> 00:02:12.270
"Enough of this eccentric
dressing, you can't,

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:13.863
can you just be elegant now you're older?"

00:02:13.863 --> 00:02:14.960
- You are elegant!

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:15.793
- Today I'm elegant.

00:02:15.793 --> 00:02:16.720
- You're so beautiful.

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:19.900
- Oh, thank you, but I
haven't, not every day.

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:21.210
- You are, you're always very elegant.

00:02:21.210 --> 00:02:22.450
- No, I'm not.

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:23.283
- Well, I think you are.

00:02:23.283 --> 00:02:24.116
- Thank you.

00:02:24.116 --> 00:02:26.860
The one thing that I thought
this was a good note from her,

00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:30.387
she said "Remember that
the cigarette holder

00:02:30.387 --> 00:02:33.267
"is as much a weapon for expression

00:02:33.267 --> 00:02:37.550
"as just satisfying my, an addiction."

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:38.540
- Oh that's, that is good.

00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:39.480
- That's pretty articulate.

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:40.313
- Yeah, yeah.

00:02:42.464 --> 00:02:43.937
- That was about it, scrub up.

00:02:43.937 --> 00:02:46.020
(laughs)

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:49.370
Scrub up, and then once I did meet her,

00:02:49.370 --> 00:02:50.670
that was another thing, I met her once,

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.440
and I do think that's pretty ironic,

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:53.310
she said to me--

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:54.143
- You did meet?

00:02:54.143 --> 00:02:55.110
- I met her years ago,
- Oh!

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:56.560
- before she died, obviously.

00:02:58.110 --> 00:02:59.197
In my early 30s, and she said

00:02:59.197 --> 00:03:01.810
"Oh, you are getting better, aren't you?"

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:03.360
and that was a, I just thought,

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:05.030
that's a very typical, now I got,

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:06.620
there's something rather
ambivalent about her,

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:09.000
she was always, she compliment,
but she'd take away, yeah.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:11.450
And she was always slightly
difficult to place,

00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:13.500
and it's that prickly sort of atmosphere.

00:03:14.610 --> 00:03:15.800
- Which is what makes her such a,

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:16.758
- She's a great
- Wonderful character

00:03:16.758 --> 00:03:17.873
- person to play.

00:03:17.873 --> 00:03:19.570
- For you to play.
- She's complicated.

00:03:19.570 --> 00:03:21.640
And she's not easy.

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:25.390
Not easy to be, I don't
think, but fun to play.

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:30.049
And you can do it many, many
ways, and be appropriate.

00:03:30.049 --> 00:03:30.882
- We don't have
- She spoke as you'd--

00:03:30.882 --> 00:03:32.150
- many ways with the
people that we're playing,

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:35.083
because, well, I couldn't
play the Queen Welsh.

00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:38.530
- You definitely couldn't play her Welsh,

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:39.797
but you could try.

00:03:39.797 --> 00:03:40.650
(laughs)

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:42.140
That is not Welsh, is it?

00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:43.300
I don't know what we are going,

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:44.676
- We're going all over Europe.

00:03:44.676 --> 00:03:46.250
- But the (speaks in a foreign language)

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:48.810
No, the Queen is, the
whole point about the Queen

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:49.994
is so consistent.

00:03:49.994 --> 00:03:50.827
- Yeah.

